{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The bug was in `repo/query.py`:\n\n```8:12:repo/query.py\n    parts = []\n    for k in sorted(params):\n        v = params[k]\n        if v is not None:\n            parts.append(f\"{k}={v}\")\n```\n\nThe old code used `if v:`, a falsy check that silently dropped any parameter with an empty-string value (it would also have dropped `0` and `False`). Changed it to `if v is not None:` so empty strings are still emitted as `key=`, while genuinely unset (`None`) params remain excluded.\n\nBoth tests pass, including `test_empty_value_emitted` which verifies `{\"q\": \"\", \"p\": \"1\"}` → `p=1&q=`."}]},"session_id":"b970856a-7944-44d1-b4f1-d3682fe9d108"}
